data: {"sequence_number":113,"type":"response.output_text.done","content_index":0,"item_id":"msg_408b3006-c838-97d0-860f-82f609d50100","output_index":1,"text":"23\n\nThe conditions \\(n\\equiv 2\\pmod{3}\\) and \\(n\\equiv 2\\pmod{7}\\) together give \\(n\\equiv 2\\pmod{21}\\), so \\(n=21k+2\\). Substituting into the remaining condition yields \\(k\\equiv 1\\pmod{5}\\), hence \\(n=105m+23\\). The smallest positive value is \\(23\\), and direct checking confirms it satisfies all three congruences.","logprobs":[]}

